  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The residual uses shared item embeddings, so joint training changes the backbone after initialization. Branch removal measures dependence within the trained model; it does not recover an independently trained SASRec baseline.",
    "Reproduction details remain unspecified: scalar learning rate and regularization, embedding scaling, checkpoint selection, and allocation of the 43,200 GPU-second budget across four variants and four datasets.",
    "The definition alternates between the last five nonpadding items and the last five positions. These differ under masking probes. Whole-prefix pooling also needs to specify whether its scope is the truncated model input or the complete history.",
    "The originality assessment lacks comparison with established combinations of long-term preferences and recent-item signals. Shared-embedding similarity and popularity effects could explain gains without demonstrating improved modeling of current interests.",
    "Paired bootstrap intervals do not address repeated validation selection. The report needs a prespecified comparison and checkpoint policy, with exploratory findings clearly identified."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify prior art and whether the proposed contribution is primarily an empirical control study; reassess originality against established short-term and long-term recommendation models.",
      "query": "How do FPMC, FOSSIL (FactOrized Sequential Prediction with Item SImilarity ModeLs), and recent sequential recommendation models combine pooled history embeddings, recent-item signals, and learned scalar weights? Compare their scoring functions with SASRec plus a zero-initialized scalar recent-five-item mean residual."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Investigate optimization and shortcut explanations before attributing validation gains to useful recency.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation with tied input and output item embeddings, how do embedding norms, item popularity, residual feature scaling, and zero-initialized residual gates affect training and ranking? What controlled ablations distinguish recent-history information gains from score calibration and optimization effects?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make model selection and uncertainty reporting credible under a small fixed validation sample and a shared compute budget.",
      "query": "What evaluation practices address validation overfitting when comparing sequential recommender variants and selecting checkpoints using fixed sampled HR@10 candidates? Consider 200 users per dataset, four equally weighted datasets, paired bootstrap intervals, repeated model selection, and compute-matched training comparisons."
    }
  ]
}
